<article class="env-lemma" id="0A9Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A9Z">Lemma <span data-tag="0A9Z">38.32.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes over $S$ with $Y$ separated and of finite type over $S$ and $X$ compactifyable over $S$. Then $X$ has a compactification over $Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $j : X \to \overline{X}$ be a compactification of $X$ over $S$. Then we let $\overline{X}'$ be the scheme theoretic image of $(j, f) : X \to \overline{X} \times _ S Y$. The morphism $\overline{X}' \to Y$ is proper because $\overline{X} \times _ S Y \to Y$ is proper as a base change of $\overline{X} \to S$. On the other hand, since $Y$ is separated over $S$, the morphism $(1, f) : X \to X \times _ S Y$ is a closed immersion (Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01KS" data-tag="01KS">26.21.10</a>) and hence $X \to \overline{X}'$ is an open immersion by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CNG" data-tag="0CNG">29.6.8</a> applied to the “partial section” $s = (j, f)$ to the projection $\overline{X} \times _ S Y \to \overline{X}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>